== Notes ==

*Added in the [[expansion pack]]s.
* Under the "Normal" and easier [[difficulty setting]]s, the petrification lasts one [[round]] per [[caster level]] when the target is a [[player character]]. Under the harder settings, and always for non-player characters, the petrification is permanent (although, as usual, all spell effects are removed when the caster rests).
* A creature whose [[appearance]] is one without flesh &mdash; or is that of a basilisk, cockatrice, medusa, or gorgon &mdash; is immune to this ability, excluding [[custom content]] appearances. (Examples of flesh-less appearances include most golems, all elementals, shadows, and skeletons. Most other skeletal appearances are also immune, with the notable exception of the normal [[lich]].)
*While the only way to specifically remove the petrification effect is with the ''stone to flesh'' spell, one can kill then [[raise dead|raise]] some victims (in particular, [[player character]]s), as this removes all effects.

